course: dictionary
lesson: 10438
title: Trout
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A trout is a fish that lives in clean, cool rivers and lakes. It is related to the salmon and often has spots on its skin.
explain: Trout can also mean the meat of the fish, which people eat. Look at the words around it to tell which meaning is right. «A boy in Ontario catches a trout, wets his hands before holding it and lets it go gently» means the fish itself, because it is caught and let go.
explain: «Mayflies are eaten by trout and other fish that leap up at them» tells you that trout eat insects. Trout are an animal in a river, not just food on a plate.
fact: A trout is a fish that lives in clean, cool rivers and lakes.
fact: Trout are related to the salmon and often have spots on their skin.
fact: Trout need lots of oxygen, so they live only where the water is clean and cool.
fact: Trout can mean the meat of the fish, which people eat.
fact: «Rainbow trout» and «brown trout» are two kinds of trout.
exercise: «A boy in Ontario catches a trout, wets his hands before holding it and lets it go gently.» What is the trout in this sentence? | Meat cooked on a plate | *A live fish that is caught and then let go | Wet hands | A bird flying over the river
exercise: «Mayflies are eaten by trout and other fish that leap up at them.» What do trout eat, according to this sentence? | Clean rivers | Pearls | *Mayflies | Gills
exercise: What kind of water do trout live in? | Hot, salty seas | Warm puddles on the road | *Clean, cool rivers and lakes | Dirty, muddy ponds
test: What is a brown trout? | *A kind of fish | A kind of mayfly | A kind of otter | A kind of mussel
test: Trout are related to which fish? | *Salmon | Shark | Cod | Herring
exam: Why do scientists use trout to check whether a river is clean? | Trout can survive in hot, dirty puddles | *Trout need lots of oxygen, so they live only in clean, cool water | Trout eat all the mud from the bottom | Trout are very noisy and show where they are
